{"name":"Peony Prize","hex":"#faddd4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"peony","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flowering plant of the genus Paeonia with large fragrant flowers.","A dark red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peony"},{"term":"prize","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["That which is taken from another; something captured; a thing seized by force, stratagem, or superior power.","Anything captured by a belligerent using the rights of war; especially, property captured at sea in virtue of the rights of war, as a vessel."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To consider highly valuable; to esteem.","To set or estimate the value of; to appraise; to price; to rate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prize"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peony","blocks":[{"text":"The peony or paeony is any flowering plant in the genus Paeonia, the only genus in the family Paeoniaceae. Peonies are native to Asia, Europe, and Western North America. Scientists differ on the number of species that can be distinguished, ranging from 25 to 40, although the current consensus describes 33 known species. The relationships between the species need to be further clarified."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/PaeoniaSuffruticosa7.jpg/330px-PaeoniaSuffruticosa7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peony","wikidata":"Q147105"},{"title":"Prize","blocks":[{"text":"A prize is an award to be given to a person or a group of people to recognize and reward their actions and achievements. Official prizes often involve monetary rewards as well as the fame that comes with them. Some prizes are also associated with extravagant awarding ceremonies, such as the Academy Awards."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Mall_culture_jakarta59.jpg/330px-Mall_culture_jakarta59.jpg?utm_source=en.wiki